--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -88,7 +88,7 @@
 
 Generation saves the training, validation and test samples and bin edges in a schema-v4 NPZ. Training reads that file; it does not regenerate it at each collision or training session. The current schema identifiers, coordinate metadata, head attribute names and random-seed derivation are retained because they specify the meaning of data and weights.
 
-Training writes its factor checkpoints and complete `v040_policy.pt` into a selected run directory. Fresh training is the default. Resume is explicit and must use the matching dataset and run directory; the inherited checkpoint identity checks still need strengthening (see CLEANUP.md).
+Option 2, **Train all heads or one selected head**, asks which head to train; leaving the selection blank trains all heads. Training writes its head checkpoints and complete `v040_policy.pt` into a selected run directory. Fresh training is the default. Resume is explicit and must use the matching dataset and run directory; the inherited checkpoint identity checks still need strengthening (see CLEANUP.md).
 
